#
# Counter-example for math:ParameterRoleCardinalityConstraint (Rule P7): a math:Distribution
# whose math:distributionParameterization math:requiresParameterRole a single rate role,
# but which supplies that role TWICE (two math:DistributionParameter nodes both carrying
# math:parameterRole ex:rateRole). The aggregate SHACL-SPARQL count-per-required-role is 2
# (!= 1), so the constraint fires — shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent
# (math:DistributionParameterRoleCardinality).
# Single violation: it names its math:distributionFamily so math:DistributionFamilyShape
# (P6a) stays SATISFIED, and it names its math:distributionParameterization so the
# parameterization gate math:DistributionParameterizationShape (P6b) stays SATISFIED —
# EXACTLY ONE finding, isolating the role-cardinality SPARQL gate.
# Back-reference: math:Distribution / math:DistributionParameterRoleCardinality (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecDistributionRoleCardinalityBad).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:overSuppliedDistribution a math:Distribution ;
    math:distributionFamily ex:poissonFamily ;
    math:distributionParameterization ex:rateParameterization ;
    math:hasDistributionParameter ex:rateParamA , ex:rateParamB .

ex:poissonFamily a math:DistributionFamily .

ex:rateParameterization a math:DistributionParameterization ;
    math:requiresParameterRole ex:rateRole .

ex:rateRole a math:DistributionParameterRole .

ex:rateParamA a math:DistributionParameter ;
    math:parameterRole ex:rateRole .

ex:rateParamB a math:DistributionParameter ;
    math:parameterRole ex:rateRole .
